1
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:19,393
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

2
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:21,313
♪ (TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

3
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:25,233
(DOOR RATTLES, CREAKS OPEN)

4
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:33,908
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

5
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:38,580
- (GRUNTS)
- ♪ (MUSIC STOPS) ♪

6
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:41,957
What the fuck?

7
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:44,460
It's time to get up, Junior.

8
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:46,296
JOHN STEWART JUNIOR:
What did the Guardians say?

9
00:00:47,589 --> 00:00:49,632
About what?

10
00:00:49,633 --> 00:00:52,718
We got four dead aliens
on a football field.

11
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:54,762
Another one just blew up
half the sheriff's station.

12
00:00:54,763 --> 00:00:56,597
Oh yeah,
I'm not calling the Guardians.

13
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:58,432
JOHN: Then what the fuck
are you doing here, Hal?

14
00:00:58,433 --> 00:01:00,143
- I'm training you.
- (BUCKET CLANGS)

15
00:01:00,644 --> 00:01:01,645
(DOOR CLOSES)

16
00:01:04,022 --> 00:01:05,065
(DOOR RATTLES)

17
00:01:08,026 --> 00:01:09,360
No, no, really.
You just take your time.

18
00:01:09,361 --> 00:01:10,611
What the fuck
are we doing, Jordan?

19
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:12,446
What're you talking about?
You've been busting my balls

20
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:13,656
for a month to learn how to fly.

21
00:01:13,657 --> 00:01:15,783
- Today's the day
you're gonna learn.
- We got a case to work.

22
00:01:15,784 --> 00:01:17,619
Jesus Christ Almighty.

23
00:01:18,244 --> 00:01:19,245
Unclench.

24
00:01:20,955 --> 00:01:22,123
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

25
00:01:26,795 --> 00:01:27,796
You ready?

26
00:01:39,641 --> 00:01:42,227
(DISTANT TRAIN HORN BLARING)

27
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:46,980
You fly.

28
00:01:46,981 --> 00:01:47,982
Fly?

29
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:51,110
- Fly.
- (CHUCKLES)

30
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:53,612
(SCOFFS) That's it?
Just... just fly?

31
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:55,906
Oh, no, no, no, no.
I-- I-- I'm sorry.

32
00:01:55,907 --> 00:01:57,241
- Fly, please.
- Ah.

33
00:01:57,242 --> 00:01:58,992
HAL JORDAN: Look,
it's supposed to be instinctual.

34
00:01:58,993 --> 00:02:00,786
Just concentrate.

35
00:02:00,787 --> 00:02:02,579
- Me, I'm a fighter pilot.
- JOHN: So I've heard.

36
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:04,331
When I think "fly,"
it's automatic.

37
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:05,709
See-- Just concentrate.

38
00:02:06,876 --> 00:02:08,669
- Think flight.
- JOHN: Mm-hmm.

39
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:10,004
Great. Thank you.

40
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:18,555
Back up a little bit.

41
00:02:19,514 --> 00:02:22,475
♪ (LOW BROODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

42
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:33,194
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

43
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:37,991
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

44
00:02:44,539 --> 00:02:46,415
(INHALES DEEPLY)

45
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:47,500
(GRUNTS)

46
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:51,546
(RING WARBLING SOFTLY)

47
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:53,964
(BIRD CHIRPING)

48
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:55,675
(WINGS FLAPPING)

49
00:02:56,718 --> 00:02:58,052
What the fuck is that?

50
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:02,222
Uh, I think that's a bird, sir.

51
00:03:02,223 --> 00:03:03,932
Uh...

52
00:03:03,933 --> 00:03:05,851
Why don't you drop
the "sir" bullshit.

53
00:03:05,852 --> 00:03:08,061
- We both know you don't mean it.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

54
00:03:08,062 --> 00:03:09,146
Whatever you say.

55
00:03:09,147 --> 00:03:10,773
(CHIRPING)

56
00:03:10,774 --> 00:03:13,192
♪ (MUSIC FADING) ♪

57
00:03:13,193 --> 00:03:16,361
- (RING PULSING)
- AUTOMATED VOICE:
<i>Ring nearing depletion.</i>

58
00:03:16,362 --> 00:03:19,073
- All right, new lesson.
Gratis. Gimme the ring.
- (RING HUMS WEAKLY)

59
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:22,243
- Come on.
- (CHIRPING)

60
00:03:23,536 --> 00:03:25,246
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

61
00:03:26,414 --> 00:03:28,248
♪ (POIGNANT MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

62
00:03:28,249 --> 00:03:29,417
Is there a problem?

63
00:03:31,294 --> 00:03:33,880
- No. No.
- ♪ (BROODING STRING
MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

64
00:03:35,507 --> 00:03:37,257
Ring gets low on charge,
there's a...

65
00:03:37,258 --> 00:03:38,967
(BIRD CHIRPING)

66
00:03:38,968 --> 00:03:40,470
...one-time trick re-up.

67
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:43,431
You just gotta...

68
00:03:44,098 --> 00:03:45,809
(CHIRPING)

69
00:03:46,726 --> 00:03:48,894
Just gotta hit it flush.

70
00:03:48,895 --> 00:03:52,105
- (RING HUMS SHARPLY)
- AUTOMATED VOICE:
<i>Ring charge, five percent.</i>

71
00:03:52,106 --> 00:03:54,274
- All right.
- ♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

72
00:03:54,275 --> 00:03:55,401
New flight plan.

73
00:03:56,736 --> 00:03:58,696
- I booked you a window.
- I don't understand.

74
00:03:59,197 --> 00:04:00,405
HAL: On an airplane.

75
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:02,407
There's seats near the windows,
there's seats near the aisles,

76
00:04:02,408 --> 00:04:03,742
and there's seats
in the middle too.

77
00:04:03,743 --> 00:04:05,661
Nobody wants those, uh--

78
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:09,122
Look, the point is I need
the lantern to charge the ring.

79
00:04:09,123 --> 00:04:11,875
I need you
to go back to Coast City
to my place and get it.

80
00:04:11,876 --> 00:04:14,294
The, uh, address is on the back
and the...

81
00:04:14,295 --> 00:04:16,129
the key is out front
under the rock.

82
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:17,798
But, Hal,
this is already booked.

83
00:04:17,799 --> 00:04:19,883
- (BIRD CHIRPING)
- (WINGS FLAPPING)

84
00:04:19,884 --> 00:04:21,802
Wait, so what would you
have done if I could fly?

85
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:24,054
Well, you didn't fly, did you?
So, it doesn't really matter.

86
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:25,974
Now get yourself ready.
I need that lantern.

87
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:28,393
Oh, uh...

88
00:04:29,769 --> 00:04:32,020
One more thing.
Uh, feed Earl for me, would you?

89
00:04:32,021 --> 00:04:34,857
- His food's in the icebox.
- And what's Earl?

90
00:04:34,858 --> 00:04:36,400
- Is it a dog? Cat?
- (CHIRPING)

91
00:04:36,401 --> 00:04:39,152
HAL: You know what?
And one more training exercise.

92
00:04:39,153 --> 00:04:42,656
Take that... that bird with you
and bring it back alive.

93
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:44,575
You lose concentration,
it disappears.

94
00:04:44,576 --> 00:04:45,994
It disappears, you fail.

95
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:48,162
Don't fail.

96
00:04:49,539 --> 00:04:50,873
(CHIRPING)

97
00:04:50,874 --> 00:04:52,332
And what are you gonna be doing?

98
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:54,836
HAL: Enjoying
not answering your questions.

99
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:57,004
(DOOR CLOSES)

100
00:04:57,005 --> 00:05:03,052
♪ (BROODING GUITAR
RIFF PLAYING) ♪

101
00:05:10,768 --> 00:05:14,022
♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

102
00:05:16,816 --> 00:05:19,319
♪ (PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

103
00:05:34,834 --> 00:05:38,546
♪ (BROODING MUSIC OVERLAPPING) ♪

104
00:05:53,269 --> 00:05:58,107
(SPRINKLERS HISSING)

105
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:03,571
♪ (INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

106
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:21,506
(CROWBAR THUDS)

107
00:06:22,256 --> 00:06:23,299
(GRILLE CLATTERS)

108
00:06:37,814 --> 00:06:40,023
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

109
00:06:40,024 --> 00:06:43,276
AUTOMATED VOICE:
<i>You've reached the Rushville
Sheriff's Department.</i>

110
00:06:43,277 --> 00:06:47,406
<i>If this is an emergency,
please hang up and dial 911.</i>

111
00:06:47,407 --> 00:06:49,157
<i>Otherwise,
please leave a message</i>

112
00:06:49,158 --> 00:06:50,951
<i>and someone
from the department...</i>

113
00:06:50,952 --> 00:06:52,912
♪ (INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

114
00:06:57,709 --> 00:06:58,960
(KEYS JINGLING)

115
00:07:09,846 --> 00:07:12,849
♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

116
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:17,645
(RING WARBLES)

117
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:24,527
♪ (LOW BROODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

118
00:07:25,486 --> 00:07:26,945
HAL: There you are.

119
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:29,156
- (RING PULSING)
- AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>This ring
will soon run out of charge.</i>

120
00:07:29,157 --> 00:07:30,323
- Fuck.
- AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Three,</i>

121
00:07:30,324 --> 00:07:32,118
<i>two, one.</i>

122
00:07:34,662 --> 00:07:36,705
- (EXHALES SHARPLY)
- (CAR DOOR CLOSES)

123
00:07:36,706 --> 00:07:39,333
- (CAR ENGINE REVVING)
- (TIRES SCREECHING)

124
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:44,172
♪ (BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

125
00:07:45,882 --> 00:07:48,342
(TIRES SCREECHING)

126
00:08:00,354 --> 00:08:03,690
(KERRY KANE SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY ON MICROPHONE)

127
00:08:03,691 --> 00:08:07,778
- (CITIZEN SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)
- (OVERLAPPING CHATTER)

128
00:08:07,779 --> 00:08:09,946
(CHATTER STOPS)

129
00:08:09,947 --> 00:08:11,532
- (DOOR HINGES CREAKING)
- ♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

130
00:08:13,409 --> 00:08:15,036
{\an8}Were you talking about me?

131
00:08:15,995 --> 00:08:18,539
- (CHAIRS CREAKING)
- (FAINT MURMURS)

132
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:20,541
You were talking about me.

133
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:30,927
(SOFTLY) Excuse me.

134
00:08:32,678 --> 00:08:33,721
Excuse me.

135
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:36,099
Excuse me.

136
00:08:38,392 --> 00:08:39,560
(CLEARS THROAT)

137
00:08:40,269 --> 00:08:43,439
(FAINT MURMURS CONTINUE)

138
00:08:43,981 --> 00:08:45,066
Carry on.

139
00:08:48,569 --> 00:08:51,738
We were just talking
about whether to go ahead

140
00:08:51,739 --> 00:08:53,574
with this Friday's
football game.

141
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:56,159
Would that be traumatizing,

142
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:59,246
{\an8}or could it help
pull the community together?

143
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:02,125
{\an8}Coach,
you were about to say something.

144
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:07,255
Right. Yeah. Um...

145
00:09:08,256 --> 00:09:09,881
I've been talking to the boys,

146
00:09:09,882 --> 00:09:13,718
and, uh,
they're pretty shook up.

147
00:09:13,719 --> 00:09:15,929
- This is also something
they've been working for...
- (QUIETLY) Hey.

148
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:17,806
- since two-a-days.
- (WHISPERS INDISTINCTLY)

149
00:09:17,807 --> 00:09:19,391
COACH: Uh, I mean... (SIGHS)

150
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:21,726
- I guess I wonder what we're...
- BILL MACON: (WHISPERS)
Sorry. Sorry.

151
00:09:21,727 --> 00:09:25,772
...what we're teaching 'em
if we just pack it up
and forfeit.

152
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:29,067
- KERRY: Yeah, I think that's
what we're trying to figure out.
- (QUIETLY) Good news.

153
00:09:29,068 --> 00:09:31,611
- I got the judge
to drop your assault charges.
- (COACH RESUMES SPEAKING)

154
00:09:31,612 --> 00:09:33,363
- Well, I appreciate that.
- (CHUCKLES)

155
00:09:33,364 --> 00:09:36,408
- How much is it gonna cost me?
- Oh, no. It's on the house.

156
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:39,286
KERRY:
And, obviously, we're worried...

157
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:42,038
Good news is you're free
to go back to Coast City.

158
00:09:42,039 --> 00:09:44,875
Or anywhere else you feel like
going for that matter.

159
00:09:44,876 --> 00:09:47,210
What was everyone talking about
when I came in here?

160
00:09:47,211 --> 00:09:49,964
KERRY: ...well-placed,
to go ahead with the game
and playing.

161
00:09:50,631 --> 00:09:52,132
Five people just died here.

162
00:09:52,133 --> 00:09:54,926
An alien blew himself up
at the sheriff's station.

163
00:09:54,927 --> 00:09:56,386
That's a lot to process.

164
00:09:56,387 --> 00:09:57,470
Did your wife tell you

165
00:09:57,471 --> 00:09:59,389
that alien was chirping
about vengeance

166
00:09:59,390 --> 00:10:01,309
before he blew himself up?

167
00:10:04,103 --> 00:10:06,480
Here's what I'd really like
to talk to you about.

168
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:09,149
I ended up
on that football field

169
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:10,650
because of a hunch. Hmm.

170
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:11,818
Just a gut feeling

171
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:13,487
that it was
gonna be extraterrestrial.

172
00:10:14,488 --> 00:10:16,782
But your father's men,
they shot four people.

173
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:21,077
And yet, those guys' friend
ends up being an alien?

174
00:10:21,078 --> 00:10:23,371
(COACH SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

175
00:10:23,372 --> 00:10:25,040
Is that a... a question or...

176
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:26,791
Uh, it's just a roundabout way
of saying

177
00:10:26,792 --> 00:10:29,212
you don't shoot people
because of a gut feeling.

178
00:10:31,088 --> 00:10:33,757
- I... I wouldn't know--
- HAL: No, I'm telling you.

179
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:35,800
- You don't.
- Okay.

180
00:10:35,801 --> 00:10:39,054
So, how is it that father's men
knew who to target?

181
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:40,430
You'd have to ask him,
I don't--

182
00:10:40,431 --> 00:10:41,681
HAL: I'm asking you
as my attorney,

183
00:10:41,682 --> 00:10:43,183
someone who cares
about my wellbeing,

184
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:44,726
and apparently,
my travel schedule.

185
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:45,852
We are still talking

186
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:47,854
with attorney-client privilege,
I presume.

187
00:10:47,855 --> 00:10:49,564
KERRY: Excuse me, honey?

188
00:10:49,565 --> 00:10:50,691
BOTH: Yes?

189
00:10:52,235 --> 00:10:53,985
KERRY: I was talking
to my husband.

190
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:55,445
Oh. Oh, yeah. Of course.

191
00:10:55,446 --> 00:10:57,781
If you two
are gonna keep talking,

192
00:10:57,782 --> 00:10:59,699
I'm gonna need
Mr. Jordan to leave.

193
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:01,785
- He started it.
- Well...

194
00:11:01,786 --> 00:11:04,205
I've got about 30 seconds
of patience left.

195
00:11:04,705 --> 00:11:05,789
I only need 40.

196
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:08,041
KERRY: And I'll be happy
to give them to you

197
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:09,377
when we're done here.

198
00:11:10,628 --> 00:11:12,255
Well, how long
is that gonna take?

199
00:11:13,631 --> 00:11:16,633
- (MICROPHONE SCREECHING)
- It'll take as long as it takes.

200
00:11:16,634 --> 00:11:19,010
Yeah, I don't think
I can keep quiet that long.

201
00:11:19,011 --> 00:11:21,388
- (CELL PHONE RINGING)
- (FAINT CHATTER)

202
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:25,017
Oh, uh, sorry,
I gotta... I gotta take this.

203
00:11:25,726 --> 00:11:27,478
Yeah. As you were.

204
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:30,146
Talk to me, Junior.

205
00:11:30,147 --> 00:11:32,315
- JOHN: This house is insane.
- (BIRD CHIRPING)

206
00:11:32,316 --> 00:11:33,817
HAL: <i>That's what you called
to tell me?</i>

207
00:11:33,818 --> 00:11:36,069
JOHN: No, no,
I can't find the key.

208
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:38,114
HAL: Well, did you look
under the rock?

209
00:11:39,907 --> 00:11:41,574
Which rock, Hal?

210
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:43,493
HAL: <i>To the left
of the door under the bush.</i>

211
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:44,744
(GRUNTS)

212
00:11:44,745 --> 00:11:46,663
- It looks like a potato
with a smile.
- (CAR ENGINE STARTING)

213
00:11:46,664 --> 00:11:49,165
HAL: Or a frown
if I left it upside down.

214
00:11:49,166 --> 00:11:50,667
Potato rock.

215
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:53,296
♪ (SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

216
00:12:00,344 --> 00:12:01,387
(KEY CLATTERS)

217
00:12:04,598 --> 00:12:05,932
(CHIRPS)

218
00:12:05,933 --> 00:12:07,184
So, how's it going over there?

219
00:12:08,394 --> 00:12:10,688
I get the feeling
everyone wants me gone.

220
00:12:12,481 --> 00:12:16,693
Kinda makes me feel
like I need to stick around.

221
00:12:16,694 --> 00:12:18,320
It would make you think that.

222
00:12:18,321 --> 00:12:20,030
HAL: <i>The lantern's in my closet.</i>

223
00:12:20,031 --> 00:12:22,533
<i>If you're at the front door,
it's upstairs to the left.</i>

224
00:12:25,953 --> 00:12:28,455
So, how much
do Lanterns get paid anyway?

225
00:12:28,456 --> 00:12:29,457
Not enough.

226
00:12:30,333 --> 00:12:31,958
I can tell you that.

227
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:35,212
- JOHN: <i>Well,
your house begs to differ.</i>
- (DOOR RATTLING)

228
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:37,172
(GLASS CLATTERING)

229
00:12:37,173 --> 00:12:39,091
- JOHN: <i>What the hell was that?</i>
- Don't worry about it.

230
00:12:40,509 --> 00:12:43,636
<i>I got the house from a rich guy.
Saved his kid.</i>

231
00:12:43,637 --> 00:12:45,972
<i>His dad felt like shit
because he couldn't help.</i>

232
00:12:45,973 --> 00:12:49,477
I didn't want to emasculate him
anymore, so I...

233
00:12:53,522 --> 00:12:54,940
let him buy me a house.

234
00:12:56,025 --> 00:12:58,402
So, when are you actually going
to move into this place?

235
00:12:59,653 --> 00:13:00,820
What are you talking about?

236
00:13:00,821 --> 00:13:03,156
I've lived in that house
for eight years.

237
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:06,159
- JOHN: <i>You've got no furniture.</i>
- (GRUNTS) I have a bed.

238
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:07,660
I found your room.

239
00:13:07,661 --> 00:13:09,829
HAL: <i>The lantern's in a box
in the back of the closet.</i>

240
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:11,499
<i>Go into the hallway
and turn right.</i>

241
00:13:12,875 --> 00:13:14,794
(PANTING)

242
00:13:20,174 --> 00:13:23,177
♪ (RIVETING INSTRUMENTAL
MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

243
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:32,686
JOHN: Hey, do you, um...

244
00:13:34,522 --> 00:13:37,273
need me to bring
a uniform back or something?

245
00:13:37,274 --> 00:13:40,026
Not unless you're gonna teach me
how someone takes a piss

246
00:13:40,027 --> 00:13:41,569
in one of those goddamn things.

247
00:13:41,570 --> 00:13:43,322
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

248
00:13:47,701 --> 00:13:49,494
(GRUNTS)

249
00:13:49,495 --> 00:13:51,037
- JOHN: <i>I see the box.</i>
- (DOORS CLOSE)

250
00:13:51,038 --> 00:13:52,163
HAL: (PANTING) <i>Good.</i>

251
00:13:52,164 --> 00:13:54,416
<i>It's voice-activated,
so when you get it next to you,</i>

252
00:13:54,417 --> 00:13:55,543
<i>put me on speaker.</i>

253
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:57,503
(GRUNTS)

254
00:13:58,629 --> 00:14:00,296
AUTOMATED VOICE:
<i>Greetings, Hal Jordan.</i>

255
00:14:00,297 --> 00:14:02,715
<i>To access the vault,
please confirm identity.</i>

256
00:14:02,716 --> 00:14:03,800
Ready.

257
00:14:03,801 --> 00:14:05,594
Mogo doesn't socialize.

258
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:08,263
(MECHANICAL WHIRRING)

259
00:14:08,264 --> 00:14:10,181
HAL: <i>Open the box.
The lantern's in there.</i>

260
00:14:10,182 --> 00:14:12,184
♪ (UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

261
00:14:17,189 --> 00:14:18,273
It's pitch-black.

262
00:14:18,274 --> 00:14:20,233
(STRAINING)
It's a pocket dimension, Junior.

263
00:14:20,234 --> 00:14:23,403
Just... just feel around
in there and...

264
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:24,988
(GRUNTS) ...you'll find it.

265
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:27,282
(BIRD CHIRPS)

266
00:14:27,283 --> 00:14:29,285
♪ (UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

267
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:33,372
(DIMENSION BOX HUMMING)

268
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:36,125
(BIRD CHIRPING DISTANTLY)

269
00:14:43,757 --> 00:14:44,884
(METALLIC CLANG)

270
00:14:45,759 --> 00:14:46,968
I got it.

271
00:14:46,969 --> 00:14:48,511
Don't forget to feed Earl.

272
00:14:48,512 --> 00:14:50,723
Spoons are on the counter.
(PANTS)

273
00:14:53,058 --> 00:14:55,936
♪ (RIVETING INSTRUMENTAL
MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

274
00:15:06,655 --> 00:15:09,115
♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

275
00:15:09,116 --> 00:15:10,117
(PANTS)

276
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:20,960
(BIRD CHIRPS)

277
00:15:20,961 --> 00:15:23,506
♪ (SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

278
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:28,427
JOHN: Earl?

279
00:15:31,722 --> 00:15:32,890
Hey, Earl.

280
00:15:33,891 --> 00:15:35,266
Dinner time.

281
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:36,352
(HAL GRUNTS)

282
00:15:38,562 --> 00:15:39,646
JOHN: <i>Earl?</i>

283
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:42,650
Got your favorite.
Uh, beef and bison.

284
00:15:52,451 --> 00:15:53,661
Earl?

285
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,334
(CHIRPING)

286
00:16:01,544 --> 00:16:04,379
Hey, Earl, listen, I, uh...
I don't know where you are,

287
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:08,675
but, um, kinda ready
to be done with this meat.

288
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:10,260
♪ (MUSIC RISES) ♪

289
00:16:10,261 --> 00:16:13,680
- (EARL GROWLS)
- (SOFTLY) Jeez!

290
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:15,223
- (BIRD SCREECHING)
- ♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

291
00:16:15,224 --> 00:16:19,185
(HISSES, GROWLS)

292
00:16:19,186 --> 00:16:20,938
What the hell is wrong
with you, Jordan?

293
00:16:22,022 --> 00:16:24,232
(EARL GROWLING)

294
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:26,443
What's up, man?
Hey, Earl. I'm, uh...

295
00:16:28,028 --> 00:16:29,905
I'm John, and I'm...
I'm here to feed you.

296
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:33,366
- Just don't eat my bird.
- (EARL GROWLS)

297
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:34,493
All right.

298
00:16:35,327 --> 00:16:37,412
- There you...
- (CHOMPS)

299
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:40,039
JOHN: You know,
uh, once upon a time,

300
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:42,041
hamburgers used
to be my thing, too.

301
00:16:42,042 --> 00:16:45,044
- (ROARS)
- Whoa! Hey!

302
00:16:45,045 --> 00:16:46,380
(BELLOWS, MUNCHES)

303
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:48,799
(CHUCKLES)

304
00:16:49,758 --> 00:16:50,926
Fucking Jordan.

305
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:54,388
(TIRES SCREECHING)

306
00:17:07,735 --> 00:17:10,070
(HAL GRUNTS)

307
00:17:13,949 --> 00:17:15,033
(FEET THUDDING)

308
00:17:15,034 --> 00:17:17,036
(GRUNTING)

309
00:17:28,631 --> 00:17:30,215
(DETECTOR CHIRPS)

310
00:17:37,389 --> 00:17:38,474
(DETECTOR CHIRPS)

311
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:42,560
- (PANTING)
- (SCANNER CHIRPS)

312
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:44,520
♪ (LOW TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

313
00:17:44,521 --> 00:17:45,648
(GROANS)

314
00:17:47,858 --> 00:17:50,819
(BIRD CHIRPING)

315
00:17:58,369 --> 00:18:00,370
(JOHN GASPS, GROANS)

316
00:18:00,371 --> 00:18:02,163
♪ (INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

317
00:18:02,164 --> 00:18:03,499
(GROANS)

318
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:05,958
(GROANS)

319
00:18:05,959 --> 00:18:07,877
(TASER CRACKLING)

320
00:18:07,878 --> 00:18:10,089
- (RUMBLING)
- ♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

321
00:18:18,138 --> 00:18:19,807
(JOHN GRUNTS)

322
00:18:23,143 --> 00:18:25,145
(PANTS)

323
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:29,983
Where are we going?

324
00:18:32,236 --> 00:18:33,696
Where's my fucking bird?

325
00:18:34,363 --> 00:18:35,406
Your bird's safe.

326
00:18:37,408 --> 00:18:38,491
(CHIRPS)

327
00:18:38,492 --> 00:18:40,993
- (ASSAILANT YELPS)
- ♪ (INTENSE MUSIC RESUMES) ♪

328
00:18:40,994 --> 00:18:42,496
(TIRES SCREECHING)

329
00:18:44,998 --> 00:18:46,333
(ASSAILANT GROANS)

330
00:18:48,043 --> 00:18:49,545
♪ (MUSIC RISES) ♪

331
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:56,176
- (GRUNTS)
- (ASSAILANT GROANS)

332
00:19:01,014 --> 00:19:02,433
(BOTH GRUNTING)

333
00:19:03,016 --> 00:19:04,226
(GROANS)

334
00:19:05,602 --> 00:19:08,230
(JOHN GROANING)

335
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:10,857
(BIRD CHIRPING)

336
00:19:10,858 --> 00:19:12,108
(BOTH YELL)

337
00:19:12,109 --> 00:19:16,613
- (CAR HORNS HONKING)
- (TIRES SCREECHING)

338
00:19:18,031 --> 00:19:20,075
♪ (INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

339
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:22,578
(CAR HORN BLARING)

340
00:19:25,289 --> 00:19:27,708
(CAR HORNS BLARING)

341
00:19:29,877 --> 00:19:31,503
(TIRES SCREECHING)

342
00:19:36,925 --> 00:19:39,969
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

343
00:19:39,970 --> 00:19:41,096
(CHIRPING)

344
00:19:48,228 --> 00:19:49,229
(DRIVER YELPS)

345
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:57,236
(TIRES SCREECHING)

346
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:59,448
- (ECHOING THUD)
- ♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

347
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:06,079
(POLICE SIREN WAILING)

348
00:20:10,459 --> 00:20:12,710
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

349
00:20:12,711 --> 00:20:15,506
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

350
00:20:22,638 --> 00:20:25,641
(CAR ENGINE RUNNING)

351
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:40,405
Is this about me
not being on the insurance?

352
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:42,698
(SNIFFS)

353
00:20:42,699 --> 00:20:44,575
It is pretty much
exactly what it looks like.

354
00:20:44,576 --> 00:20:45,827
But in my defense,

355
00:20:45,828 --> 00:20:47,829
I wanted to talk to you
about this at the meeting,

356
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:48,872
and you shushed me.

357
00:20:50,207 --> 00:20:53,167
You're killing me, Jordan.
You know that?

358
00:20:53,168 --> 00:20:56,170
Just a slow, painful death.

359
00:20:56,171 --> 00:20:58,756
There's more going on here
than you realize.

360
00:20:58,757 --> 00:21:01,175
You mean like you going
to the stadium

361
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:04,011
and dragging these corpses
through the metal detector,

362
00:21:04,012 --> 00:21:07,558
which you now realize
is actually an alien detector?

363
00:21:08,433 --> 00:21:10,142
Uh, let me rephrase.

364
00:21:10,143 --> 00:21:13,521
You obviously realize
exactly what's going on here.

365
00:21:13,522 --> 00:21:16,649
Congratulations.
You've caught up to me.

366
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:19,318
Now, would you just please
let me do my job?

367
00:21:19,319 --> 00:21:21,696
Is this a good time
to talk about jurisdiction?

368
00:21:21,697 --> 00:21:22,864
Because you seemed
really hung up

369
00:21:22,865 --> 00:21:24,240
on what was terrestrial
and what wasn't.

370
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:26,617
- And as far as--
- Where are you going
with these guys?

371
00:21:26,618 --> 00:21:27,911
To visit your father-in-law.

372
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:35,001
May I just say,
that is a profoundly bad idea.

373
00:21:35,002 --> 00:21:37,503
Did he put up those detectors?

374
00:21:37,504 --> 00:21:39,422
- He did.
- Do you know where he got them?

375
00:21:39,423 --> 00:21:41,257
- I do not.
- You're not even curious?

376
00:21:41,258 --> 00:21:44,093
It's not against the law
to be obsessed with aliens.

377
00:21:44,094 --> 00:21:45,678
Trust me, I wish it was.

378
00:21:45,679 --> 00:21:48,014
It'd make my marriage
a hell of a lot smoother.

379
00:21:48,015 --> 00:21:49,265
Your marriage is unsmooth?

380
00:21:49,266 --> 00:21:53,144
The fact is, Macon hasn't done
anything illegal.

381
00:21:53,145 --> 00:21:55,855
Now, he was cordial
when he needed you,

382
00:21:55,856 --> 00:21:57,315
but if you show up today

383
00:21:57,316 --> 00:22:00,610
with all your questions
and all your attitude,

384
00:22:00,611 --> 00:22:02,404
it is not gonna go well.

385
00:22:03,614 --> 00:22:04,698
Whose side are you on?

386
00:22:07,451 --> 00:22:10,287
- ♪ (BROODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪
- (SNIFFS, EXHALES SHARPLY)

387
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:17,753
I'll take you,
but you let me do the talking.

388
00:22:18,837 --> 00:22:20,630
Understood?

389
00:22:20,631 --> 00:22:23,050
- Well, I don't know if I--
- Just nod.

390
00:22:25,844 --> 00:22:26,887
KERRY: Follow me.

391
00:22:27,763 --> 00:22:29,306
♪ (BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

392
00:22:39,983 --> 00:22:40,983
Hey, Ben.

393
00:22:40,984 --> 00:22:42,611
I'd like to see
your boss, please.

394
00:22:44,488 --> 00:22:47,239
I'm afraid
he's not accepting visitors.

395
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:49,742
Yeah, I get that. Absolutely.

396
00:22:49,743 --> 00:22:51,661
You know, sometimes
you just gotta accept things

397
00:22:51,662 --> 00:22:53,288
that take you
out of your comfort zone.

398
00:22:54,581 --> 00:22:56,165
Is he speaking for you?

399
00:22:56,166 --> 00:22:58,918
Right now,
he's pretty much just speaking.

400
00:22:58,919 --> 00:23:01,505
This is part of
an official investigation, son.

401
00:23:02,798 --> 00:23:05,424
- Is that true?
- Evidently.

402
00:23:05,425 --> 00:23:07,260
Well, in that case,
can I see your warrant?

403
00:23:10,013 --> 00:23:12,683
Well, look at that. The cavalry.
Just in the nick of time.

404
00:23:16,561 --> 00:23:17,604
(HORSE NEIGHS)

405
00:23:20,107 --> 00:23:22,775
The calvary's a lot faster
in the movies.

406
00:23:22,776 --> 00:23:24,861
I told them
you aren't seeing any visitors.

407
00:23:25,737 --> 00:23:28,115
That's okay, Ben. Hey, Kerry.

408
00:23:29,282 --> 00:23:31,283
You know I'm a fan of your work.

409
00:23:31,284 --> 00:23:33,870
But I confess, I'm confused
as to why you're still in town.

410
00:23:34,538 --> 00:23:35,871
Four aliens are dead.

411
00:23:35,872 --> 00:23:37,624
Their accomplice
blew himself up.

412
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:39,750
And yet, you linger.

413
00:23:39,751 --> 00:23:41,752
Well, that's what
your son told me.

414
00:23:41,753 --> 00:23:44,381
But, uh...
Well, here's what I think.

415
00:23:46,008 --> 00:23:47,633
I think you're hiding something
on this property

416
00:23:47,634 --> 00:23:48,718
you don't want me to see.

417
00:23:48,719 --> 00:23:50,636
I had you as a guest here
just the other day.

418
00:23:50,637 --> 00:23:51,971
Because you wanted me to prove

419
00:23:51,972 --> 00:23:53,973
that that fella
in custody was an alien.

420
00:23:53,974 --> 00:23:56,308
Which you did. Like I said,
I'm a fan of your work,

421
00:23:56,309 --> 00:23:58,144
- but your work here's done.
- Oh, I just need a minute

422
00:23:58,145 --> 00:23:59,645
- of your time.
- I believe you've had it.

423
00:23:59,646 --> 00:24:01,856
♪ (LOW TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

424
00:24:01,857 --> 00:24:03,941
Front gate, eleven o'clock.

425
00:24:03,942 --> 00:24:06,485
(RADIO BEEPING)

426
00:24:06,486 --> 00:24:08,529
Oh, boy.
Am I about to be threatened?

427
00:24:08,530 --> 00:24:10,823
I got four dead bodies in my car

428
00:24:10,824 --> 00:24:12,742
that set off
the hidden camera and alarm

429
00:24:12,743 --> 00:24:14,493
when I drag 'em
through those metal detectors

430
00:24:14,494 --> 00:24:16,787
you got set up
at the stadium there.

431
00:24:16,788 --> 00:24:20,166
Now, I don't want to disparage
your small, little town,

432
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:21,500
but I've been
all over the galaxy,

433
00:24:21,501 --> 00:24:23,210
and I don't think
I've ever seen technology

434
00:24:23,211 --> 00:24:24,379
quite that sophisticated.

435
00:24:25,922 --> 00:24:26,923
I told you.

436
00:24:27,966 --> 00:24:31,010
People who walked this land
before me,

437
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:33,054
they got caught flat-footed
when the settlers come in

438
00:24:33,055 --> 00:24:34,764
and colonized 'em.

439
00:24:34,765 --> 00:24:36,724
I'm not about to make
that same mistake again.

440
00:24:36,725 --> 00:24:38,684
And how about that technology?

441
00:24:38,685 --> 00:24:40,936
Very generous gift from the man
who funds this property.

442
00:24:40,937 --> 00:24:42,521
- Oh, your benefactor?
- WILL MACON: Correct.

443
00:24:42,522 --> 00:24:43,939
Tell me the truth.
Is he even real,

444
00:24:43,940 --> 00:24:45,608
or is this some
Keyser Söze situation?

445
00:24:45,609 --> 00:24:46,984
Oh, I assure you,
he's very real.

446
00:24:46,985 --> 00:24:48,152
HAL:
Then what's his name again?

447
00:24:48,153 --> 00:24:49,361
I'm not at liberty to say.

448
00:24:49,362 --> 00:24:51,113
- Because of the NDA.
- WILL: That's right.

449
00:24:51,114 --> 00:24:52,239
That's-- You know,

450
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:54,283
- do all cowboys have NDAs...
- That's it.

451
00:24:54,284 --> 00:24:55,993
- We're leaving.
- ...or are you just
a special cowboy?

452
00:24:55,994 --> 00:24:57,078
No, I'm serious.

453
00:24:57,079 --> 00:25:00,206
You got this whole Marlboro Man
thing happening here,

454
00:25:00,207 --> 00:25:02,750
but yet you can't be straight
with me because of an NDA?

455
00:25:02,751 --> 00:25:04,376
Hell, even that other guy,

456
00:25:04,377 --> 00:25:06,045
he was selling cigarettes
to kids,

457
00:25:06,046 --> 00:25:07,963
and he still didn't let
those lawyers stop him

458
00:25:07,964 --> 00:25:09,800
from saying
whatever the hell he wanted.

459
00:25:13,386 --> 00:25:15,346
I want to know
what other technology you got

460
00:25:15,347 --> 00:25:16,722
in this compound.

461
00:25:16,723 --> 00:25:18,891
I think
it's important for you to know

462
00:25:18,892 --> 00:25:20,643
there's a man with a rifle
in that guard tower

463
00:25:20,644 --> 00:25:22,103
with instructions
to shoot anybody

464
00:25:22,104 --> 00:25:23,355
who trespasses on this property.

465
00:25:24,731 --> 00:25:26,233
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

466
00:25:27,275 --> 00:25:28,568
Well, you can't do that.

467
00:25:31,113 --> 00:25:34,740
- Can he do that?
- He can absolutely do that.

468
00:25:34,741 --> 00:25:36,243
Well, that just seems
unneighborly.

469
00:25:36,827 --> 00:25:37,911
Sheriff.

470
00:25:38,745 --> 00:25:39,829
HAL: I'm coming on.

471
00:25:39,830 --> 00:25:41,540
You're gonna have to deal
with me.

472
00:25:42,415 --> 00:25:44,416
Oh, for Christ's sake,
I got the ring.

473
00:25:44,417 --> 00:25:46,585
You try to shoot me,
and I'm just gonna put up--

474
00:25:46,586 --> 00:25:47,878
♪ (MUSIC STOPS ABRUPTLY) ♪

475
00:25:47,879 --> 00:25:51,091
- (CHAIR RATTLING)
- (JOHN BREATHING HEAVILY)

476
00:25:57,180 --> 00:25:59,182
I apologize for the violence.

477
00:26:01,059 --> 00:26:03,269
- (BIRD CHIRPING)
- Yeah.

478
00:26:03,270 --> 00:26:06,898
May I ask you a question
about the bird, John Stewart?

479
00:26:07,941 --> 00:26:08,941
Sure.

480
00:26:08,942 --> 00:26:10,609
It's a wildly
impressive construct,

481
00:26:10,610 --> 00:26:12,278
but how does
Hal Jordan continue

482
00:26:12,279 --> 00:26:14,322
to project it
from such a great distance?

483
00:26:15,907 --> 00:26:17,993
He's not projecting it. I am.

484
00:26:18,952 --> 00:26:20,119
You're not wearing a ring.

485
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:22,288
Did you tie me up
to ask me questions

486
00:26:22,289 --> 00:26:23,414
about my fucking bird?

487
00:26:23,415 --> 00:26:26,168
No, I tied you up
to ask you about Manhunters.

488
00:26:31,506 --> 00:26:33,340
I'm sorry.
Was I supposed to react?

489
00:26:33,341 --> 00:26:34,466
Yeah, you are.

490
00:26:34,467 --> 00:26:36,635
Because you think
I know what a Manhunter is?

491
00:26:36,636 --> 00:26:38,137
ANTAAN: Given your proximity
to Hal Jordan,

492
00:26:38,138 --> 00:26:39,763
it'd be very hard
to believe that you do not.

493
00:26:39,764 --> 00:26:41,432
Proximity. You mean "closeness"?

494
00:26:41,433 --> 00:26:44,310
That's a better word, yes.
That's a much better word.

495
00:26:44,311 --> 00:26:47,105
JOHN: I see human
isn't your first language here.

496
00:26:48,190 --> 00:26:51,150
I'm not even close
to close with Hal Jordan.

497
00:26:51,151 --> 00:26:53,736
In fact, he sent me here
to get rid of me,

498
00:26:53,737 --> 00:26:55,070
so I'm sorry, gentlemen.

499
00:26:55,071 --> 00:26:56,363
♪ (FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

500
00:26:56,364 --> 00:26:57,907
But you're about to torture
a man

501
00:26:57,908 --> 00:26:59,201
who doesn't know shit.

502
00:26:59,951 --> 00:27:05,664
(LAUGHS)

503
00:27:05,665 --> 00:27:07,083
Torture? No, John.

504
00:27:07,918 --> 00:27:09,252
We don't want
to torture you, John.

505
00:27:10,003 --> 00:27:11,171
We want to recruit you.

506
00:27:13,423 --> 00:27:15,759
You don't tell someone
when you wanna recruit them.

507
00:27:16,843 --> 00:27:18,719
You have to be more subtle.

508
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:20,346
ANTAAN: We don't have time
for subtlety, John.

509
00:27:20,347 --> 00:27:22,640
One of the most dangerous beings
to ever exist

510
00:27:22,641 --> 00:27:24,725
knows it has been found,
which means right now

511
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:26,186
it is preparing
its brutal response.

512
00:27:27,187 --> 00:27:28,520
And that's a Manhunter?

513
00:27:28,521 --> 00:27:30,356
You think the Green Lanterns
came first?

514
00:27:30,357 --> 00:27:32,566
- You really don't know?
- I really don't know.

515
00:27:32,567 --> 00:27:34,151
Well, that makes things
much easier.

516
00:27:34,152 --> 00:27:35,486
I don't have to change
your mind.

517
00:27:35,487 --> 00:27:36,820
I just need to stamp it.

518
00:27:36,821 --> 00:27:38,240
What the fuck
do you mean, stamp?

519
00:27:41,451 --> 00:27:43,994
Imprint? Um...

520
00:27:43,995 --> 00:27:46,706
- Enlighten.
- I don't need enlightenment.

521
00:27:48,208 --> 00:27:51,210
There was a time of chaos
in the galaxy.

522
00:27:51,211 --> 00:27:53,963
- Then the Manhunters came.
- (MECHANISM CLICKING)

523
00:27:53,964 --> 00:27:55,422
ANTAAN: We don't know
where they came from,

524
00:27:55,423 --> 00:27:56,716
just that they were synthetic.

525
00:27:57,717 --> 00:27:59,051
And able to build new bodies,

526
00:27:59,052 --> 00:28:01,095
which meant they could take
the form of any species

527
00:28:01,096 --> 00:28:04,307
and embed, undetected,
within any society.

528
00:28:05,100 --> 00:28:06,767
This ability to build
allowed them

529
00:28:06,768 --> 00:28:08,185
to invent technologies

530
00:28:08,186 --> 00:28:11,063
far beyond the limits
of the planets they inhabited.

531
00:28:11,064 --> 00:28:14,233
They were brutal.
They were deceptive.

532
00:28:14,234 --> 00:28:16,987
They carried out
what they called "justice."

533
00:28:18,029 --> 00:28:19,905
Entire species were lost.

534
00:28:19,906 --> 00:28:20,948
(DEVICE CLICKS, HUMS)

535
00:28:20,949 --> 00:28:22,741
ANTAAN: And then,
as mysteriously as they arrived,

536
00:28:22,742 --> 00:28:23,951
they were gone.

537
00:28:23,952 --> 00:28:25,995
At least
we thought they were gone.

538
00:28:25,996 --> 00:28:28,747
In reality, one of them remained
on our planet,

539
00:28:28,748 --> 00:28:29,748
passing as one of us

540
00:28:29,749 --> 00:28:31,876
while he quietly engineered
a holocaust.

541
00:28:33,378 --> 00:28:35,171
Have you ever been deceived
by someone you love?

542
00:28:36,589 --> 00:28:37,798
Yeah.

543
00:28:37,799 --> 00:28:39,884
Then you'll understand
when you experience

544
00:28:40,969 --> 00:28:42,512
what he did to us.

545
00:28:45,432 --> 00:28:48,100
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

546
00:28:48,101 --> 00:28:49,352
(CHIRPING)

547
00:28:51,855 --> 00:28:54,482
Get off. (GRUNTS)

548
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:58,444
I'm sorry, but you need to see.

549
00:28:58,445 --> 00:29:01,363
- (DEVICE BUZZING)
- (GROANS)

550
00:29:01,364 --> 00:29:03,449
- ♪ (OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING) ♪
- (SCREAMS)

551
00:29:03,450 --> 00:29:04,950
ANTAAN: This is what
it looks like

552
00:29:04,951 --> 00:29:07,287
when a Manhunter
destroys your people.

553
00:29:08,830 --> 00:29:10,914
John, do you see
what it feels like?

554
00:29:10,915 --> 00:29:12,249
(JOHN SOBS)

555
00:29:12,250 --> 00:29:14,626
- ANTAAN: See it!
- (GROANS)

556
00:29:14,627 --> 00:29:16,795
ANTAAN: Do you see
what it did to them, John?

557
00:29:16,796 --> 00:29:20,090
- Do you see it?
- (SCREAMS)

558
00:29:20,091 --> 00:29:21,134
ANTAAN: See it!

559
00:29:22,302 --> 00:29:24,928
♪ (MUSIC RISES) ♪

560
00:29:24,929 --> 00:29:26,513
- (DEVICE TURNS OFF)
- ♪ (MUSIC FALLS) ♪

561
00:29:26,514 --> 00:29:27,599
(PANTS)

562
00:29:30,477 --> 00:29:32,979
♪ (PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

563
00:29:36,858 --> 00:29:38,401
(GRUNTS)

564
00:29:42,155 --> 00:29:45,074
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

565
00:29:45,075 --> 00:29:46,992
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

566
00:29:46,993 --> 00:29:48,827
The effects
of our collective loss

567
00:29:48,828 --> 00:29:50,538
will remain with you
for some time.

568
00:29:51,664 --> 00:29:52,874
I'm sorry.

569
00:29:58,421 --> 00:30:00,130
The scale of our tragedy
drew the attention

570
00:30:00,131 --> 00:30:02,217
of a Green Lantern
sent by the Guardians.

571
00:30:03,301 --> 00:30:05,220
The Lantern

572
00:30:06,346 --> 00:30:08,013
took the monster
into his custody

573
00:30:08,014 --> 00:30:09,766
and guaranteed
he'd be executed.

574
00:30:12,143 --> 00:30:14,396
- Why?
- ANTAAN: I do not know.

575
00:30:15,355 --> 00:30:16,563
It does not matter,

576
00:30:16,564 --> 00:30:18,650
but we believed, somewhere,
the Manhunter was still alive.

577
00:30:20,110 --> 00:30:24,655
So, we searched, John.
We searched for years.

578
00:30:24,656 --> 00:30:26,741
Until finally we discovered
where he was hiding.

579
00:30:28,618 --> 00:30:29,743
Rushville.

580
00:30:29,744 --> 00:30:31,703
ANTAAN:
Our detection is limited.

581
00:30:31,704 --> 00:30:33,872
There's radiation unique
to the Manhunter,

582
00:30:33,873 --> 00:30:35,707
though he could be disguised
as any human.

583
00:30:35,708 --> 00:30:37,794
To find out which,
we had to get close.

584
00:30:38,711 --> 00:30:40,839
But our team was exposed
and killed.

585
00:30:43,550 --> 00:30:45,009
And who should arrive
an hour later?

586
00:30:45,718 --> 00:30:46,719
Jordan.

587
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:49,763
You think he was trying
to protect the thing?

588
00:30:49,764 --> 00:30:51,014
ANTAAN: Perhaps.

589
00:30:51,015 --> 00:30:53,225
Our target knows
we've located him.

590
00:30:53,226 --> 00:30:55,727
And we cannot enter Rushville
without being detected.

591
00:30:55,728 --> 00:30:58,647
♪ (LOW TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

592
00:30:58,648 --> 00:30:59,691
So, you...

593
00:31:01,067 --> 00:31:03,069
you must identify the Manhunter.

594
00:31:05,905 --> 00:31:07,739
How the fuck
am I supposed to do that?

595
00:31:07,740 --> 00:31:08,907
Your bird.

596
00:31:08,908 --> 00:31:10,994
This bird is proof
you can achieve the impossible.

597
00:31:12,245 --> 00:31:14,455
Now, we could fulfill
our mission

598
00:31:14,456 --> 00:31:17,124
by walking into the town square
and detonating ourselves,

599
00:31:17,125 --> 00:31:19,002
but that would destroy
Rushville.

600
00:31:20,545 --> 00:31:23,297
No reason for innocent lives
to be lost.

601
00:31:23,298 --> 00:31:26,342
Because it took a human form,
it could be killed as a human.

602
00:31:27,010 --> 00:31:28,970
You have 48 hours, John.

603
00:31:31,222 --> 00:31:32,432
Find the Manhunter.

604
00:31:36,478 --> 00:31:37,520
Once you do...

605
00:31:39,439 --> 00:31:41,148
contact us.

606
00:31:41,149 --> 00:31:43,109
- If you fail to contact us--
- Yeah, I got it.

607
00:31:46,738 --> 00:31:48,405
♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

608
00:31:48,406 --> 00:31:51,201
- (INHALES SHARPLY)
- (MONITOR BEEPING)

609
00:31:57,707 --> 00:31:58,791
KERRY: Hey, there.

610
00:32:02,212 --> 00:32:03,505
They shot me.

611
00:32:05,298 --> 00:32:07,341
KERRY: You were trespassing.

612
00:32:07,342 --> 00:32:09,051
Might as well have walked
onto that ranch

613
00:32:09,052 --> 00:32:10,803
with a sign
that said, "Shoot me."

614
00:32:12,472 --> 00:32:15,474
- How are you feeling?
- Uh, all right.

615
00:32:15,475 --> 00:32:17,852
A little sore.
How long have I been out?

616
00:32:18,937 --> 00:32:21,772
Not too long.
They cleared you to go.

617
00:32:21,773 --> 00:32:23,900
Just wanted you
to sleep off the anesthesia.

618
00:32:25,068 --> 00:32:28,321
(PANTS)

619
00:32:32,242 --> 00:32:33,284
So...

620
00:32:34,410 --> 00:32:36,538
what's with Sinestro?

621
00:32:38,081 --> 00:32:39,541
Why are you asking me that?

622
00:32:40,833 --> 00:32:43,086
KERRY: You kept saying his name
in your sleep.

623
00:32:45,255 --> 00:32:46,923
I'm not authorized
to talk about that.

624
00:32:48,591 --> 00:32:51,010
It's not exactly top secret.

625
00:32:53,096 --> 00:32:57,599
It says here, "He was a Lantern,
attempted a coup,

626
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:59,686
killed one of the bosses."

627
00:33:00,895 --> 00:33:03,856
It also says you were the one
who took him down.

628
00:33:08,152 --> 00:33:09,987
I don't talk about that.

629
00:33:09,988 --> 00:33:13,241
Except that you do,
in your sleep.

630
00:33:14,325 --> 00:33:15,451
- How...
- (HANDCUFF RATTLES)

631
00:33:18,454 --> 00:33:20,247
You gotta be kidding me.

632
00:33:20,248 --> 00:33:22,916
Like I said,
you were trespassing.

633
00:33:22,917 --> 00:33:24,334
HAL: In the name of Tom Osborne,

634
00:33:24,335 --> 00:33:26,086
or whoever it is
that you worship,

635
00:33:26,087 --> 00:33:28,046
please take these off.

636
00:33:28,047 --> 00:33:32,176
Not until you listen to me.
Can you manage that?

637
00:33:32,885 --> 00:33:35,054
- Yes, ma'am.
- Good.

638
00:33:36,055 --> 00:33:38,056
Because every time
you don't listen,

639
00:33:38,057 --> 00:33:39,516
or you steal bodies,

640
00:33:39,517 --> 00:33:42,269
or storm
my father-in-law's compound

641
00:33:42,270 --> 00:33:45,731
and don't let me do the talking,
what you're really doing

642
00:33:45,732 --> 00:33:47,942
is cutting my legs
straight out from under me.

643
00:33:49,068 --> 00:33:51,069
I'm the sheriff.

644
00:33:51,070 --> 00:33:54,323
If you don't follow my lead,
you're legitimizing this idea

645
00:33:54,324 --> 00:33:57,327
that Macon is the seat of power.
And trust me,

646
00:33:58,328 --> 00:34:00,997
you do not want to help
push that narrative.

647
00:34:02,749 --> 00:34:04,374
This is my town.

648
00:34:04,375 --> 00:34:07,127
I have worked my ass off
to earn people's respect,

649
00:34:07,128 --> 00:34:09,172
and I can't have you
undermining that.

650
00:34:12,592 --> 00:34:13,676
You're right.

651
00:34:16,429 --> 00:34:18,431
I'm sorry. You're right.

652
00:34:23,394 --> 00:34:25,228
So, you're gonna go back
to your motel

653
00:34:25,229 --> 00:34:26,522
and let me do my job?

654
00:34:27,273 --> 00:34:29,859
No more storming the compound?

655
00:34:31,527 --> 00:34:33,696
I swear on Tom Osborne's life.

656
00:34:49,671 --> 00:34:51,129
(HANDCUFF UNLOCKS)

657
00:34:51,130 --> 00:34:53,840
And for the record,
I'm not on your side.

658
00:34:53,841 --> 00:34:56,260
I'm not on Macon's side.
I'm on my side,

659
00:34:57,136 --> 00:34:58,971
trying to hold
this town together.

660
00:35:03,643 --> 00:35:04,644
(SIGHS)

661
00:35:07,647 --> 00:35:09,815
Can I ask you a question?

662
00:35:09,816 --> 00:35:12,067
If I knew
about the alien detectors,

663
00:35:12,068 --> 00:35:13,986
why did I fight you
on jurisdiction?

664
00:35:14,987 --> 00:35:16,322
Does make a guy wonder.

665
00:35:18,991 --> 00:35:21,159
The others were dead.

666
00:35:21,160 --> 00:35:23,620
I assumed if Waylon
didn't set off the alarm,

667
00:35:23,621 --> 00:35:24,872
he wasn't an alien.

668
00:35:25,915 --> 00:35:26,999
I was wrong.

669
00:35:28,042 --> 00:35:29,085
It happens.

670
00:35:30,128 --> 00:35:31,921
KERRY: It shouldn't. Look.

671
00:35:32,964 --> 00:35:35,717
I apologize
for trying to obstruct you.

672
00:35:37,176 --> 00:35:39,302
I just didn't want Billy's dad

673
00:35:39,303 --> 00:35:41,221
insurrecting the shit
out of everyone

674
00:35:41,222 --> 00:35:44,517
and getting them all paranoid
about invasion.

675
00:35:45,727 --> 00:35:47,186
So much for that plan.

676
00:35:50,356 --> 00:35:52,024
Thanks for being straight
with me.

677
00:35:54,485 --> 00:35:57,195
Thanks for not dying
in my jurisdiction.

678
00:35:57,196 --> 00:35:58,197
(CHUCKLES DRYLY)

679
00:36:00,700 --> 00:36:02,201
KERRY: My turn for a question.

680
00:36:03,870 --> 00:36:06,205
Why am I still in town
if the threat's over?

681
00:36:07,331 --> 00:36:08,957
It does make a girl wonder.

682
00:36:08,958 --> 00:36:12,044
Something is off here.
I can feel it.

683
00:36:16,090 --> 00:36:17,675
Why do you want me gone?

684
00:36:19,051 --> 00:36:21,636
Everything feels
like it's about to explode

685
00:36:21,637 --> 00:36:23,097
for no good reason.

686
00:36:24,140 --> 00:36:26,100
This place is losing its mind.

687
00:36:27,310 --> 00:36:30,396
You kicking up dust
and getting shot isn't helping.

688
00:36:33,065 --> 00:36:35,151
If I need you, I can call.

689
00:36:40,406 --> 00:36:41,824
You were at my bedside.

690
00:36:43,701 --> 00:36:45,786
It's a great book.

691
00:36:45,787 --> 00:36:48,331
It's hard to find time
to read with a kid at home.

692
00:36:50,708 --> 00:36:54,754
- (TELEPHONE RINGING)
- ♪ (BROODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

693
00:37:06,641 --> 00:37:10,144
(SIGHS) So,
where are you from, anyway?

694
00:37:11,604 --> 00:37:13,563
You decide
to actually make nice,

695
00:37:13,564 --> 00:37:16,316
and that's the best you got?
"Where you from?"

696
00:37:16,317 --> 00:37:18,443
Well, you don't exactly
scream Rushville.

697
00:37:18,444 --> 00:37:21,489
- (SCOFFS) You're a snob.
- Doesn't mean I'm wrong.

698
00:37:22,782 --> 00:37:26,368
I'm from Gotham.
Moved here on a whim.

699
00:37:26,369 --> 00:37:28,955
- That sounds like a story.
- Doesn't it?

700
00:37:30,832 --> 00:37:33,417
- That's all I'm gonna get?
- Pretty much.

701
00:37:34,001 --> 00:37:36,336
Hmm. I'll take it for now.

702
00:37:36,337 --> 00:37:38,713
KERRY:
Because you're not leaving.

703
00:37:38,714 --> 00:37:40,966
You didn't hear a word I said
in there, did you?

704
00:37:40,967 --> 00:37:43,927
Well, I heard a few of 'em.
Where are all the patients?

705
00:37:43,928 --> 00:37:46,888
It's a small town,
not exactly a big patient pool.

706
00:37:46,889 --> 00:37:48,640
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

707
00:37:48,641 --> 00:37:50,141
(SIGHS)

708
00:37:50,142 --> 00:37:51,226
Half the equipment looks

709
00:37:51,227 --> 00:37:52,978
like it was just taken out
of the crate.

710
00:37:52,979 --> 00:37:54,604
Yeah, well,
mostly everyone's smart enough

711
00:37:54,605 --> 00:37:56,107
not to get themselves shot.

712
00:37:57,608 --> 00:38:00,194
- (THUNDER RUMBLES)
- ♪ (BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

713
00:38:07,785 --> 00:38:09,328
JOHN: Thank you.
Just over here is great.

714
00:38:15,334 --> 00:38:16,752
There you go. Thank you.

715
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:20,714
- (BELL RINGING)
- (BIRD CHIRPS)

716
00:38:20,715 --> 00:38:23,383
♪ (SOFT COUNTRY MUSIC PLAYING
OVER SPEAKERS) ♪

717
00:38:23,384 --> 00:38:25,468
(FAINT CHATTER)

718
00:38:25,469 --> 00:38:26,512
(DOOR CLOSES)

719
00:38:30,016 --> 00:38:31,850
- (DOOR OPENS)
- (BELL RINGING)

720
00:38:31,851 --> 00:38:33,185
(GROANS) Hey.

721
00:38:34,020 --> 00:38:36,229
- Um, can I get a...
- (DOOR CLOSES)

722
00:38:36,230 --> 00:38:38,148
I... I'll get a decaf, please.
Thank you.

723
00:38:38,149 --> 00:38:40,275
- SERVER: Of course.
- (BIRD TWEETS)

724
00:38:40,276 --> 00:38:41,693
(COOKWARE CLANKING)

725
00:38:41,694 --> 00:38:44,196
- (JOHN SIGHS)
- (DOOR HINGES CREAKING)

726
00:38:52,413 --> 00:38:54,540
It's a small town,
bound to happen.

727
00:38:57,126 --> 00:38:58,126
Yeah.

728
00:38:58,127 --> 00:39:00,379
ZOE MACON: The booths
are more comfortable.

729
00:39:01,714 --> 00:39:03,757
Uh, it's been a long day.

730
00:39:03,758 --> 00:39:06,801
I'm just trying to clear my head
for a second.

731
00:39:06,802 --> 00:39:08,637
Yeah, yeah. Fair enough.

732
00:39:08,638 --> 00:39:11,390
- (COFFEE POURING)
- (THUNDER RUMBLING)

733
00:39:15,061 --> 00:39:16,144
Thank you very much.

734
00:39:16,145 --> 00:39:17,396
- Here you go.
- JOHN: Thanks.

735
00:39:19,231 --> 00:39:22,234
(BIRD TWEETING)

736
00:39:42,922 --> 00:39:44,131
(SIGHS)

737
00:39:45,591 --> 00:39:48,094
Um, for the record,

738
00:39:49,512 --> 00:39:51,847
I wouldn't have slept with you
if I knew you were married.

739
00:39:55,184 --> 00:39:57,103
Well, I'm glad you didn't know.

740
00:39:59,313 --> 00:40:01,272
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

741
00:40:01,273 --> 00:40:02,733
You into that kind of thing?

742
00:40:04,110 --> 00:40:05,569
ZOE: What kind of thing is that?

743
00:40:07,530 --> 00:40:08,906
I mean, uh...

744
00:40:10,324 --> 00:40:12,118
is your relationship
unconventional?

745
00:40:16,122 --> 00:40:17,372
You've met my husband, right?

746
00:40:17,373 --> 00:40:18,456
- JOHN: Mm-hmm.
- Mm-hmm.

747
00:40:18,457 --> 00:40:20,000
Yeah. What do you think?

748
00:40:20,001 --> 00:40:22,711
Uh, respectfully? I think
he's pretty fucking weird.

749
00:40:22,712 --> 00:40:25,380
(LAUGHS) Yeah, that he is.
Deeply so.

750
00:40:25,381 --> 00:40:27,132
Yeah. I think
he's pretty fucking weird,

751
00:40:27,133 --> 00:40:28,134
but you're not.

752
00:40:29,635 --> 00:40:30,636
(CUP CLINKS)

753
00:40:31,679 --> 00:40:35,682
- How can you be so sure?
- Uh, I see you. Um...

754
00:40:35,683 --> 00:40:37,559
I don't think
you would do anything

755
00:40:37,560 --> 00:40:40,145
without thinking about it first.
You know?

756
00:40:40,146 --> 00:40:43,941
White men have the privilege
of being eccentric.

757
00:40:45,151 --> 00:40:47,193
White men with money?

758
00:40:47,194 --> 00:40:49,780
They can do
whatever the fuck they want.

759
00:40:50,448 --> 00:40:53,450
Play cowboy, build castles.

760
00:40:53,451 --> 00:40:56,911
- Do you like that?
- ZOE: Yeah. I like the security.

761
00:40:56,912 --> 00:40:58,413
I also like
that he could've bought

762
00:40:58,414 --> 00:41:00,457
some blonde bimbo from Texas
to be his arm candy,

763
00:41:00,458 --> 00:41:01,584
but he wanted me.

764
00:41:02,918 --> 00:41:04,794
I'm sure a lot
of people want you.

765
00:41:04,795 --> 00:41:05,796
ZOE: None...

766
00:41:07,506 --> 00:41:09,050
that could give me what he has.

767
00:41:10,593 --> 00:41:11,676
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

768
00:41:11,677 --> 00:41:13,387
It's a lot to deal with,
I know, but...

769
00:41:14,346 --> 00:41:15,765
but it's worth it, I think.

770
00:41:16,849 --> 00:41:19,726
And when I need a break,
I just take one.

771
00:41:19,727 --> 00:41:22,187
So, you'll put up with some
deeply weird White man

772
00:41:22,188 --> 00:41:24,439
with a savior complex
just to live the life?

773
00:41:24,440 --> 00:41:26,859
No, I'm with my husband
because I love him.

774
00:41:28,027 --> 00:41:29,528
And I know he loves me.

775
00:41:33,783 --> 00:41:35,283
Hey, how's your White man?

776
00:41:35,284 --> 00:41:36,452
(CHUCKLES)

777
00:41:37,119 --> 00:41:39,413
Uh, how is he?

778
00:41:40,956 --> 00:41:42,290
He wanted me out the way,

779
00:41:42,291 --> 00:41:44,835
so he, uh... he sent me
to fetch his things.

780
00:41:50,466 --> 00:41:53,385
Is that why you were trying
to clear your head over there?

781
00:41:57,848 --> 00:41:58,891
Uh...

782
00:42:00,935 --> 00:42:03,561
I'm just trying to figure out
if I can trust him.

783
00:42:03,562 --> 00:42:05,855
ZOE: If you have to ask
the question,

784
00:42:05,856 --> 00:42:08,317
then you already know
the answer.

785
00:42:12,071 --> 00:42:14,156
(CAR ENGINE RUMBLING)

786
00:42:22,331 --> 00:42:25,084
(BIRD CHIRPING)

787
00:42:34,260 --> 00:42:37,012
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

788
00:42:38,180 --> 00:42:39,265
JOHN: Nope.

789
00:42:41,016 --> 00:42:42,226
Don't.

790
00:42:47,189 --> 00:42:48,274
What happened to you?

791
00:42:48,983 --> 00:42:50,316
Your girlfriend's husband

792
00:42:50,317 --> 00:42:52,277
sicced one of you sniper-types
on me.

793
00:42:52,278 --> 00:42:54,738
- Oh. Shoulder?
- HAL: Mm-hmm.

794
00:42:55,656 --> 00:42:57,448
Through and through?

795
00:42:57,449 --> 00:42:59,576
Yeah, it's a nice warning shot.

796
00:42:59,577 --> 00:43:01,286
Good to know
you're a fan of his work.

797
00:43:01,287 --> 00:43:03,539
- Yeah.
- (HAL GRUNTS)

798
00:43:05,291 --> 00:43:08,794
- (DISTANT TRAIN HORN BLARING)
- (ZIPPER OPENS)

799
00:43:13,883 --> 00:43:15,634
I told you
not to bring the suit.

800
00:43:16,594 --> 00:43:18,553
Yeah, well,
maybe I couldn't bring myself

801
00:43:18,554 --> 00:43:20,013
to just disrespect it.

802
00:43:20,014 --> 00:43:21,723
What else were you doing
while you were rummaging

803
00:43:21,724 --> 00:43:23,057
through my stuff?

804
00:43:23,058 --> 00:43:25,853
Dance around in my bathrobes?
Sing into my hairbrush?

805
00:43:28,189 --> 00:43:29,230
(LANTERN WHIRRING)

806
00:43:29,231 --> 00:43:30,899
HAL: "In brightest day,
in blackest night,

807
00:43:30,900 --> 00:43:32,108
no evil shall escape my sight.

808
00:43:32,109 --> 00:43:33,484
Let those who worship
evil's might

809
00:43:33,485 --> 00:43:35,278
beware my power,
Green Lantern's light."

810
00:43:35,279 --> 00:43:37,363
- (WHIRRING STOPS)
- (SIGHS)

811
00:43:37,364 --> 00:43:39,158
There's something
on that compound.

812
00:43:39,950 --> 00:43:41,326
Benefactor's the key.

813
00:43:41,327 --> 00:43:43,745
We're not leaving here
until we find out who he is

814
00:43:43,746 --> 00:43:44,996
and what they're hiding.

815
00:43:44,997 --> 00:43:46,664
Yeah.

816
00:43:46,665 --> 00:43:49,710
- Whatever you say.
- (BIRD CHIRPING)

817
00:43:52,338 --> 00:43:54,464
HAL: Hey, you might want to, uh,

818
00:43:54,465 --> 00:43:56,884
check the fine print
on that insurance policy.

819
00:44:11,565 --> 00:44:13,733
What the hell's
all over the seats?

820
00:44:13,734 --> 00:44:17,029
I believe, uh, technically
they call that alien goo.

821
00:44:18,447 --> 00:44:19,448
(CAR DOOR CLOSES)

822
00:44:22,701 --> 00:44:23,744
(CAR DOOR SLAMS SHUT)

823
00:44:25,996 --> 00:44:26,996
(CHUCKLES)

824
00:44:26,997 --> 00:44:29,541
♪ (LOW TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

825
00:44:40,052 --> 00:44:41,720
What do you know
about Manhunters?

826
00:44:45,224 --> 00:44:46,474
Where'd you hear that word?

827
00:44:46,475 --> 00:44:49,727
Our buddy Waylon had friends.
They followed me onto the plane,

828
00:44:49,728 --> 00:44:51,729
snatched me outside
of your house.

829
00:44:51,730 --> 00:44:53,106
They're convinced
there's a Manhunter

830
00:44:53,107 --> 00:44:54,191
here in Rushville.

831
00:44:55,234 --> 00:44:56,402
(HAL GRUNTS)

832
00:45:00,489 --> 00:45:03,241
So, what did they want with you?

833
00:45:03,242 --> 00:45:07,787
They want me to ID him.
And give him a call in 48 hours.

834
00:45:07,788 --> 00:45:10,623
Otherwise, they'll blow up
half of western Nebraska.

835
00:45:10,624 --> 00:45:11,833
Why you?

836
00:45:11,834 --> 00:45:15,044
Because they don't trust you.
In fact, he made it explicit

837
00:45:15,045 --> 00:45:16,879
that I shouldn't tell you
any of this.

838
00:45:16,880 --> 00:45:18,798
- What else?
- JOHN: Just that he thinks

839
00:45:18,799 --> 00:45:21,301
the Guardians
may have hid the Manhunter here.

840
00:45:21,302 --> 00:45:24,095
- They wouldn't do that.
- Well, shit. That's what I said.

841
00:45:24,096 --> 00:45:26,306
I knew there was something
about this place.

842
00:45:26,307 --> 00:45:28,350
And my gut is never wrong.

843
00:45:31,228 --> 00:45:32,604
(BIRD CHIRPING)

844
00:45:36,650 --> 00:45:38,318
Abin Sur must have brought
him here

845
00:45:38,319 --> 00:45:39,695
and the Manhunter killed him.

846
00:45:40,904 --> 00:45:42,364
Yeah, and then you got
your ring.

847
00:45:43,490 --> 00:45:45,783
What else can you tell me
about Manhunters?

848
00:45:45,784 --> 00:45:47,243
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

849
00:45:47,244 --> 00:45:48,703
It's above
your pay grade, Junior.

850
00:45:48,704 --> 00:45:51,831
JOHN: No, it's not.
I told you he was here.

851
00:45:51,832 --> 00:45:54,500
Oh, so now Mr. Chain of Command
wants me to break the rules?

852
00:45:54,501 --> 00:45:56,294
Hal, they don't know
what form he's taken.

853
00:45:56,295 --> 00:45:58,797
He could be anyone in town.

854
00:46:00,090 --> 00:46:01,717
♪ (MUSIC INTENSIFIES) ♪

855
00:46:02,384 --> 00:46:03,677
What else did they say to you?

856
00:46:06,805 --> 00:46:08,307
You know, just that, um,

857
00:46:09,475 --> 00:46:11,060
to create a living thing,

858
00:46:12,227 --> 00:46:15,480
let alone keeping it alive
while not wearing the ring,

859
00:46:15,481 --> 00:46:16,981
is so advanced

860
00:46:16,982 --> 00:46:18,649
that it's practically
impossible.

861
00:46:18,650 --> 00:46:21,110
But I figured
that couldn't be true,

862
00:46:21,111 --> 00:46:23,112
'cause if it was,

863
00:46:23,113 --> 00:46:25,199
you would've at least given me
a hoorah.

864
00:46:27,242 --> 00:46:28,494
Hoorah.

865
00:46:34,917 --> 00:46:36,168
Forty-eight hours, huh?

866
00:46:37,961 --> 00:46:39,629
Yeah, 48.

867
00:46:39,630 --> 00:46:41,340
You tell the Guardians
any of this?

868
00:46:42,424 --> 00:46:44,343
(BIRD CHIRPING)

869
00:46:44,885 --> 00:46:46,220
JOHN: I report to you.

870
00:46:48,055 --> 00:46:49,598
- Hey.
- What?

871
00:46:51,266 --> 00:46:52,683
HAL:
What's with that bird, anyway?

872
00:46:52,684 --> 00:46:53,768
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

873
00:46:53,769 --> 00:46:55,603
- What are you talking about?
- The bird.

874
00:46:55,604 --> 00:46:57,563
I mean, you brought it to life
with your subconscious.

875
00:46:57,564 --> 00:46:59,607
It must mean
something pretty deep.

876
00:46:59,608 --> 00:47:00,692
It's just a bird.

877
00:47:01,860 --> 00:47:04,696
(CHIRPS)

878
00:47:05,322 --> 00:47:06,532
(CONSTRUCT WARBLES)

879
00:47:12,204 --> 00:47:16,874
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

880
00:47:16,875 --> 00:47:20,963
(DOOR OPENS, CLOSES)

881
00:47:24,091 --> 00:47:27,177
♪ (FAST-TEMPO
SYNTH MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

882
00:47:31,432 --> 00:47:32,516
(LANTERN CLANGS)

883
00:47:46,405 --> 00:47:49,199
♪ (DRAMATIC
SYNTH MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

884
00:47:58,750 --> 00:48:01,753
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

885
00:48:20,647 --> 00:48:22,316
(CLANGING HUM)

886
00:48:24,318 --> 00:48:25,736
(CLANGING HUM)

887
00:48:29,323 --> 00:48:30,448
(DOOR HUMS)

888
00:48:30,449 --> 00:48:32,408
- Authorize Hal Jordan.
- ♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

889
00:48:32,409 --> 00:48:33,702
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Access granted.</i>

890
00:48:35,871 --> 00:48:38,874
(CELL DOOR WHIRRING)

891
00:48:54,973 --> 00:48:55,974
Sinestro.

892
00:48:57,643 --> 00:48:58,644
Hal.

893
00:49:00,229 --> 00:49:02,104
Tell me what you know
about Manhunters.

894
00:49:02,105 --> 00:49:03,814
♪ ("HUMAN CONDITION"
BY PRETTY SICK PLAYING) ♪

895
00:49:03,815 --> 00:49:06,860
No hello?
No how have I been?

896
00:49:07,861 --> 00:49:09,738
HAL: Hello, Sinestro,
how have you been?

897
00:49:11,198 --> 00:49:13,325
Now, what the fuck do you know
about Manhunters?

898
00:49:14,660 --> 00:49:16,245
If one still existed,

899
00:49:17,120 --> 00:49:18,663
it'd be the second
greatest threat

900
00:49:18,664 --> 00:49:19,998
you're currently facing.

901
00:49:21,917 --> 00:49:23,960
So why don't you tell me
about John Stewart?

902
00:49:23,961 --> 00:49:26,880
♪ ("HUMAN CONDITION"
CONTINUES PLAYING) ♪

903
00:49:32,302 --> 00:49:34,762
<i>♪ She takes my hand
And she pours me a glass ♪</i>

904
00:49:34,763 --> 00:49:37,056
<i>♪ Addiction's a disease
So, I get a pass ♪</i>

905
00:49:37,057 --> 00:49:42,687
<i>♪ I wanna feel something again ♪</i>

906
00:49:42,688 --> 00:49:45,356
<i>♪ She takes my hand
And she asks me to dance ♪</i>

907
00:49:45,357 --> 00:49:47,567
<i>♪ Nothing really matters
If you don't have romance ♪</i>

908
00:49:47,568 --> 00:49:53,490
<i>♪ I wanna feel something again ♪</i>

909
00:50:03,875 --> 00:50:06,043
<i>♪ He takes me out and says
"Let's do business" ♪</i>

910
00:50:06,044 --> 00:50:08,713
<i>♪ He's a bad guy
But I believe in forgiveness ♪</i>

911
00:50:08,714 --> 00:50:13,051
<i>♪ I wanna do something
That matters ♪</i>

912
00:50:14,428 --> 00:50:16,470
<i>♪ Takes a meeting
'Cause he likes my vision ♪</i>

913
00:50:16,471 --> 00:50:19,181
<i>♪ I'm not opportunistic
No, I'm just ambitious ♪</i>

914
00:50:19,182 --> 00:50:25,063
<i>♪ I wanna be someone
That matters ♪</i>

915
00:50:45,334 --> 00:50:47,835
<i>♪ The freedom you're being sold
Is just submission ♪</i>

916
00:50:47,836 --> 00:50:50,671
<i>♪ They wanna keep you content
And under supervision ♪</i>

917
00:50:50,672 --> 00:50:53,215
<i>♪ They got you convinced
That ignorance is bliss in ♪</i>

918
00:50:53,216 --> 00:50:56,510
<i>♪ Some ever changing mind
Erasing human condition ♪</i>

919
00:50:56,511 --> 00:51:02,183
<i>♪ I don't have time
To worry about ♪</i>

920
00:51:02,184 --> 00:51:07,271
<i>♪ If I am stuck
And if there's any way out ♪</i>

921
00:51:07,272 --> 00:51:17,532
<i>♪ I don't have time ♪</i>

922
00:51:18,992 --> 00:51:20,619
♪ (SONG CONCLUDES) ♪
